   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "Rewrite with sine and cosine: \\( \\sec{\\left(x \\right)} = \\frac{1}{\\cos{\\left(x \\right)}} \\) and \\( \\cot{\\left(x \\right)} = \\frac{\\cos{\\left(x \\right)}}{\\sin{\\left(x \\right)}} \\).",
         "rule_named": "rewrite over sine and cosine"
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "Apply the quotient rule to each piece and simplify the numerators with \\( \\sin^{2} x + \\cos^{2} x = 1 \\): the derivatives are \\( \\tan{\\left(x \\right)} \\sec{\\left(x \\right)} \\) and \\( - \\csc^{2}{\\left(x \\right)} \\).",
         "rule_named": "quotient rule and a Pythagorean identity"
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "So \\( h'(x) = 2 \\tan{\\left(x \\right)} \\sec{\\left(x \\right)} + \\csc^{2}{\\left(x \\right)} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Add",
            [
               "Multiply",
               2,
               [
                  "Tan",
                  "x"
               ],
               [
                  "Sec",
                  "x"
               ]
            ],
            [
               "Power",
               [
                  "Csc",
                  "x"
               ],
               2
            ]
         ],
         "rule_named": "constant multiple and sum rules"
      },
      {
         "step": 4,
         "text": "At \\( x = \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\), \\( h'\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right) = 2 + 2 \\sqrt{2} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Add",
            2,
